From 106f4c314523541569c9513e090241f3a91be108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:40:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): cache toolpath overlay lines and regions across
 frames

A selected or previewed 8100-move Offset path cost about 9-11 ms of
CPU on each still frame. The overlay cloned the path and built its
lines again, measured the solid extent again for the chevron arm,
and built the operation region two times per frame. The op page and
the browser also cloned the whole path to read its warnings.

- path_overlay: the path lines are kept per operation under their
  inputs (path signature, warnings, palette, ground, dim, arm). The
  chevron arm is kept under each model's facets and pose. Moved out
  of interact.rs.
- frame_memo: the region is kept across frames under the operation
  value and its op_stamp. The Pocket page note reads it too.
- model::with_toolpath reads the path with no clone.

Fixes #2201

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
